===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|pt|China}},<ref>{{w|Duarte Barbosa}}, ''[https://web.archive.org/web/20230405161732/https://bndigital.bnportugal.gov.pt/indexer/index/livro/aut/PT/45458.html Descrição das Terras da India Oriental...]'', c. 1516.</ref><ref>{{w|Garcia de Orta}}, ''{{w|Colóquios dos simples e drogas da India|Colóquios dos Simples e Drogas da India}}'', 1563.</ref> probably under influence from {{der|en|fro|Chin}},<ref>{{w|Marco Polo}} & al., {{w|The Travels of Marco Polo|Divisiment dou Monde}}<!--sic-->, c. 1298.</ref> from {{der|en|fa-cls|چین|tr=čīn}}, from {{der|en|pal|𐭰𐭩𐭭||China|tr=Čīn}}, from {{der|en|sa|चीन|t=the [[Chinese]]; China}} of uncertain etymology. It is usually thought to be derived from {{der|en|zh|秦}} ([[Standard Mandarin|{{smallcaps|sm}}]] ''Qín'', [[Middle Chinese|{{smallcaps|mc}}]] ''d͡ziɪn'', [[Old Chinese|{{smallcaps|oc}}]] ''*zin'', "[[Qin]]"), the westernmost {{w|states of ancient China|ancient Chinese state}},<ref name="Singh"/><ref name="Mayrhofer"/><ref name="Yule"/> but other theories have been proposed, including derivation from {{m|zh|晉}} ([[Standard Mandarin|{{smallcaps|sm}}]] ''Jìn'', [[Middle Chinese|{{smallcaps|mc}}]] ''t͡siɪn'', [[Old Chinese|{{smallcaps|oc}}]] ''*ʔsins'', "[[Jin]]"), another important ancient state;<ref name="Zhengzhang"/> {{m|zh|荊}} ([[Standard Mandarin|{{smallcaps|sm}}]] ''Jīng'', [[Middle Chinese|{{smallcaps|mc}}]] ''kˠiæŋ'', [[Old Chinese|{{smallcaps|oc}}]] ''*keŋ'', "[[Chu]]"), the southernmost ancient Chinese state;<ref name="Wade"/> or ''Zina'', the endonym of the people of the [[Yelang]] kingdom.<ref name="Wade"/> See "[[w:Names of China|Names of China]]" and "[[Chinas]]" at [[w:Main Page|Wikipedia]]. As a female name, usually derived via {{m|en|china||[[porcelain]]}} and {{m|en|china doll}}, ultimately from the same source.

